@startuml

title 08. Inventory documents and stock movements

hide circle
skinparam linetype ortho

enum InventoryDocumentType {
	purchase_receipt
	sale_shipment
	customer_return
	supplier_return
	production
	write_off
	stock_adjustment
	transfer
	reversal
}

enum InventoryDocumentStatus {
	draft
	posted
	canceled
}

enum InventoryReasonType {
	write_off
	stock_adjustment
	return
	production_loss
	transfer
	initial_stock
	inventory_count
	damage
	other
}

enum InventoryDirection {
	in
	out
}

entity InventoryDocument {
	* id: int
	--
	* number: string(255)
	* type: InventoryDocumentType
	* status: InventoryDocumentStatus
	* documentDate: DateTimeImmutable
	currency: Currency?
	exchangeRateToBase: decimal(18,8)?
	totalAmount: decimal(14,4)?
	totalAmountBase: decimal(14,4)?
	postedAt: DateTimeImmutable?
	canceledAt: DateTimeImmutable?
	comment: text?
	* createdAt: DateTimeImmutable
	* updatedAt: DateTimeImmutable
	* store: Store
	createdBy: User?
	updatedBy: User?
	postedBy: User?
	canceledBy: User?
	reversedDocument: InventoryDocument?
	order: Order?
	purchase: Purchase?
	productionOrder: ProductionOrder?
	reason: InventoryReason?
}

entity InventoryReason {
	* id: int
	--
	* name: string(255)
	* type: InventoryReasonType
	* status: ActiveStatusEnum
	* createdAt: DateTimeImmutable
	* updatedAt: DateTimeImmutable
	deletedAt: DateTimeImmutable?
	* store: Store
	createdBy: User?
	updatedBy: User?
}

entity InventoryDocumentLine {
	* id: int
	--
	* quantity: decimal(14,4)
	unitPrice: decimal(14,4)?
	unitPriceBase: decimal(14,4)?
	totalPrice: decimal(14,4)?
	totalPriceBase: decimal(14,4)?
	* direction: InventoryDirection
	* inventoryDocument: InventoryDocument
	* product: Product
	* warehouse: Warehouse
	warehouseStock: WarehouseStock?
	orderEntry: OrderEntry?
	purchaseEntry: PurchaseEntry?
}

entity StockMovement {
	* id: int
	--
	* quantityChange: decimal(14,4)
	* unitCost: decimal(14,4)
	balanceAfter: decimal(14,4)?
	* createdAt: DateTimeImmutable
	* inventoryDocumentLine: InventoryDocumentLine
	* warehouseStock: WarehouseStock
	warehouseStockBatch: WarehouseStockBatch?
}

Store ||--o{ InventoryDocument : owns
InventoryDocumentType ||--o{ InventoryDocument : classifies
InventoryDocumentStatus ||--o{ InventoryDocument : controls
InventoryReasonType ||--o{ InventoryReason : classifies
Store ||--o{ InventoryReason : defines
InventoryReason |o--o{ InventoryDocument : explains
Currency |o--o{ InventoryDocument : document currency
InventoryDocument |o--o{ InventoryDocument : reverses
InventoryDocument ||--o{ InventoryDocumentLine : has lines
InventoryDirection ||--o{ InventoryDocumentLine : defines
InventoryDocumentLine ||--o{ StockMovement : posts movements
Product ||--o{ InventoryDocumentLine : moved as
Warehouse ||--o{ InventoryDocumentLine : used in
WarehouseStock ||--o{ InventoryDocumentLine : affected by
WarehouseStock ||--o{ StockMovement : changes by
WarehouseStockBatch |o--o{ StockMovement : batch detail
Order ||--o{ InventoryDocument : generates stock docs
Purchase ||--o{ InventoryDocument : generates stock docs
ProductionOrder ||--o{ InventoryDocument : generates stock docs
OrderEntry |o--o{ InventoryDocumentLine : ships/returns
PurchaseEntry |o--o{ InventoryDocumentLine : receives/returns
User |o--o{ InventoryDocument : creates/updates/posts/cancels

note right of InventoryDocument
  Current project status:
  - InventoryDocument, InventoryDocumentLine, StockMovement
    and InventoryReason are implemented.
  - InventoryPostingService posts document lines into
    WarehouseStock and StockMovement records.
  - Posted document cancellation creates and posts a reversal.
  - Purchase receipt and sale shipment update business
    progress through 08.1 services.

  Implemented behavior:
  - draft = editable and has no stock effect.
  - posted = immutable and creates movements.
  - canceled = canceled through reversal logic, not destructive edits.
  - only one of order or purchase is filled.
  - postedBy/postedAt and canceledBy/canceledAt are filled by workflow.
  - posted documents are corrected by reversal documents.
  - currency fields are optional for purely technical documents.

  Remaining integration:
  - ProductionOrder is not implemented yet.
  - InventoryReason CRUD/validation can be expanded for UI workflows.
  - transfer and production document flows are later stages.
end note

note right of InventoryReason
  Required behavior:
  - Dictionary for consistent grouping and reporting of stock reasons.
  - Useful examples: damage, write-off, inventory count,
    initial stock, customer return, production loss.
  - Suggested uniqueness: store + type + name.
end note

note right of InventoryDocumentLine
  Required behavior:
  - quantity > 0; direction defines IN/OUT.
  - monetary fields follow InventoryDocument currency when present.
  - sale_shipment uses OUT; purchase_receipt uses IN.
  - customer_return uses IN; supplier_return uses OUT.
  - transfer uses paired OUT/IN lines.
  - One business line can be represented by multiple document lines
    over time for partial operations.
end note

note right of StockMovement
  Required behavior:
  - Created only from posted document lines.
  - quantityChange is signed: IN > 0, OUT < 0.
  - Movements are append-only after posting.
  - OUT must not make WarehouseStock.quantityOnHand negative.
  - unitCost is stored in Store.baseCurrency.
  - average_cost uses a posting-time cost snapshot;
    fifo may split one line into several batch movements.
end note

note bottom
  Implementation status:

  Done:

  1. Added entities/enums/repositories for documents, reasons,
     lines and movements.
  2. Added InventoryPostingService:
     post(document), cancel(document), createReversal(document).
  3. Implemented stock_adjustment posting foundation.
  4. Implemented purchase_receipt and sale_shipment flows.
  5. Added reversal, non-negative stock and average-cost tests.
  6. Continued with 08.1 synchronization.

  Deferred:

  7. Add transfer and production document flows later.
  8. Expand InventoryReason validation for adjustment/write-off
     UI workflows.

  This is the central stock module.
end note

@enduml
